    <comment>New package: gpscorrelate 2.3

GPS Correlate stamps the location from a GPX track into the EXIF GPS tags of
digital photos taken at the same time. It has been maintained in Application:Geo
and is submitted to Factory now that it is on a current upstream release with a
working regression test suite (203 cases, run in %check).

The package is split into the command line tool (gpscorrelate), the GTK
interface (gpscorrelate-gui) and the HTML manual (gpscorrelate-doc), matching
Debian's layout, so the CLI does not pull in GTK. Licence is GPL-2.0-or-later
per the source headers. Builds clean on x86_64 and aarch64, rpmlint 0/0/0.</comment>
    <requestid>1370627</requestid>
